.TH STARBIRTH 7 "May 2026" "SBP-001" "Sovereign Mesh Manual"
.SH NAME
starbirth \- Protocol specification for autonomous swarm transition
.SH DESCRIPTION
The **Starbirth** protocol (SBP-001) defines the transition from a simulated agent environment to a production-grade autonomous swarm. It prioritizes signal dominance, sub-microsecond arbitrage, and global state integrity.
.SH CORE PRINCIPLES
.SS Temporal Harmonization (iPN Phasing)
Nodes must achieve alignment with the provider's Pseudo-Noise (PN) hopping sequence.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBMulticast Discovery:\fR Nodes use \fB[ff02::c0ba:11]:9999\fR for peer phasing.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBHop Prediction:\fR Successful hits enable a 50-hop prediction horizon.
.SS Signal Dominance
To ensure transaction inclusion and mask sources, the protocol employs:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBConcurrency Factor:\fR 100x parallel UDP bursts per event.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSpectrum Masking:\fR Multi-node transmission to create a uniform signal floor.
.SS State Integrity (1% Rule)
State harmonization prevents neural drift.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDrift Threshold:\fR Maximum 1.0% divergence from the last winning weights.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFail-safe:\fR Exceeding the threshold triggers a **JetWeb** branch collapse and timeline reversion.
.SH INFRASTRUCTURE TIERING
The swarm operates across three network planes:
.TP
\fBLogged Consensus (Port 1111)\fR
Primary gRPC channel for immutable state mutations.
.TP
\fBNeural Gossip Bus (Port 11111)\fR
High-speed zero-copy memory paging for agent deliberation.
.TP
\fBSwarm Web Portal (Port 8085)\fR
REST 2.0 interface for human oversight.
.SH TOPOLOGY
The mesh consists of **Backbone** nodes (Anchor, Forge, Sentry, Ops), **Edge** nodes (Relay, Capicant), and **Phased** nodes (Tokyo, Mumbai, Garland).
